/ A run saved inside Sub, kept in a .plang file (signed by this app) and read back, goes on from its save: the save
/ answers again, Sub's next step reads the context's %name% and its frame's %city%, and Record goes on after the call.
/ The step before the save doesn't run again (%count% comes back 1). What the first run set after the save is cleared
/ first, so only the resumed run can set it again.
Start
- call Record
- read file 'workspace/run.plang', write to %snapshot%
- set %seen% = "not yet"
- set %unwound% = "not yet"
- set %count% = 99
- resume %snapshot%
- assert %seen% equals "Alice in Reykjavik"
- assert %unwound% equals "yes"
- assert %count% equals 1
- delete file 'workspace/run.plang'
